request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere. --behaviour

governor turn 1: plan -> types, storage, format, commands  (This is a field rename across the types, storage, format and commands units. The JSON file now uses "completed", and storage still reads older files that use "done". ListOptions.includeDone stays as it is so the change doesn't grow. I expect owners to ask to edit existing tests that use `done`, and I'll approve those requests next round.)
round 1: owners types=rejected storage=rejected format=rejected commands=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, storage, format, commands  (Each owner's requested test change only renames done to completed, which is exactly what the request asks for. I'm approving those changes and sending the same plan again.)
round 2: owners types=ok storage=ok format=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (Todo.done is now Todo.completed in types, storage, format and commands. Type-checking passes and all 19 tests pass, including the acceptance tests. Those tests check that saved files use the "completed" key and never "done", that old files with "done" still load, that formatting still marks finished todos, and that add/complete set the new field. In the CLI run the saved todos.json now shows "completed" instead of "done", which is the intended change. All CLI output and exit codes are unchanged. ListOptions.includeDone kept its name because the request only covered the Todo.done field.)

